## Your PO Review Flow

I'll use **QuickForm** — it's inline, no extra deployment step needed, and ideal for approval tasks.

Since the flow starts from a manual trigger, the PO data will be passed in when the flow is kicked off (e.g. by an upstream automation or a scheduled job that reads POs from your ERP/email). The reviewer will see the PO details in Action Center and click Approve or Reject.

---

## Proposed Schema — Please Confirm Before I Write Anything

**Form title:** Purchase Order Review

**What the reviewer sees (read-only context):**

| Field | Label | Type |
|---|---|---|
| `ponumber` | PO Number | string |
| `vendorname` | Vendor Name | string |
| `totalamount` | Total Amount | number |
| `description` | Description / Purpose | string |
| `requestedby` | Requested By | string |

**What the reviewer fills in:**

| Field | Label | Type | Required |
|---|---|---|---|
| `comments` | Comments | string | No |

**Action buttons:**

| Button | Role | Flow effect |
|---|---|---|
| ✅ **Approve** | Primary | Flow continues |
| ❌ **Reject** | Secondary | Flow ends |
| 🔄 **Request More Info** | Neutral | Flow ends (sends back for more detail) |

**Task settings:** Priority = Low · Timeout = 24 hours (defaults)

---

